B.afr=new A.I4(!0,"# Privacy Policy \u2014 Specrails\n\nSpecrails Companion controls and observes an approved Specrails Desktop. Desktop runs the agents; the phone does not run AI models.\n\n## Connection and access\n\nPairing requires approval on Desktop. A short-lived signaling mailbox exchanges connection information to establish encrypted WebRTC communication. Project RPCs and live updates travel over the data channel rather than through the signaling mailbox. Network/ICE services may receive connection metadata.\n\nDesktop validates the device token and current project grants. Missions require an all-projects grant because a pinned project is context, not an agent security boundary. Pair only devices you trust, and revoke access in Desktop when needed.\n\n## Stored and displayed data\n\n- **Credentials.** Native platforms use secure storage such as Keychain/Keystore; web uses the secure-storage plugin\u2019s WebCrypto-backed browser storage. Tokens are sent to Desktop to authorize requests.\n- **Read cache.** Specs, Rails and other ordinary project reads may be stored in browser/native preferences for offline viewing. Unpairing, changing Desktop identity or a permission denial clears this cache.\n- **Missions.** Mission transcripts are displayed from live snapshots and are not added to the persistent read cache. The last received state can remain in memory while offline; revocation or a Desktop change clears it.\n- **Project content.** Conversations and application logs may contain sensitive project information. Known filesystem/credential metadata and raw provider tool inputs are excluded from the mobile contract, but arbitrary text may still contain sensitive content.\n- **Camera.** Camera access is used to scan the pairing QR code. Companion does not upload those camera frames as mission attachments.\n- **Accounts and tracking.** Companion does not require its own account and does not include advertising or behavioral analytics SDKs.\n\nThe AI providers configured on Desktop have their own data policies. Consult the current privacy information on specrails.dev for the public website and connection services.\n\n## Contact\n\nQuestions? Open an issue at github.com/fjpulidop or write to the address listed on specrails.dev.\n",!1,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,B.Hb,B.Hc,!0,B.Hk,!0,null)
